§ `Schedule 1 - taking or destroying fish`

-- src:281 | 2 Taking or destroying fish
-- src:282 | (1) A person who unlawfully takes or destroys, or attempts to take or destroy, any fish in water which is private property or in which there is any private right of fishery shall on summary conviction be liable to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
-- src:283 | (2) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:284 | (3) The court by which a person is convicted of an offence under sub-paragraph (1) above may order the forfeiture of anything which, at the time of the offence, he had with him for use for taking or destroying fish.
-- src:285 | (4) Any person may arrest without warrant anyone who is, or whom he, with reasonable cause, suspects to be, committing an offence under sub-paragraph (1) above, and may seize from any person who is, or whom he, with reasonable cause, suspects to be, committing any offence under this paragraph anything which on that person’s conviction of the offence would be liable to be forfeited under sub-paragraph (3) above.
@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2 (src:281-285)
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`Sch 1 para 2(1) penalty for taking or destroying fish` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `the section states no imprisonment`
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1) (src:282)
GIVEN f IS A `Fish facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` f MEANS
        f's `he unlawfully took or destroyed fish, or attempted to`
    AND f's `the fish were in water which is private property or in which there is a private right of fishery`

@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1) (src:282)
GIVEN f IS A `Fish facts`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
`Sch 1 para 2(1) liable on summary conviction for taking or destroying fish` f MEANS
    IF `Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` f
    THEN `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `Sch 1 para 2(1) penalty for taking or destroying fish`
    ELSE `no offence under this section on these facts`

@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2(3) (src:284)
GIVEN f IS A `Fish facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 2(3) the court may order forfeiture of the thing he had with him` f MEANS
        `Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` f
    AND f's `he has been convicted of that offence`
    AND f's `the thing was with him at the time for use for taking or destroying fish`

@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2(4) (src:285)
GIVEN f IS A `Fish facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may arrest him without warrant` f MEANS
    f's `the other person is committing an offence under paragraph 2(1), or the person acting with reasonable cause suspects he is`

@ref Theft Act 1968 Schedule 1 paragraph 2(4) (src:285)
GIVEN f IS A `Fish facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may seize the thing from him` f MEANS
        f's `the other person is committing an offence under paragraph 2(1), or the person acting with reasonable cause suspects he is`
    AND f's `the thing is one that would be liable to forfeiture on the other's conviction`
